Subject: =?UTF-8?q?=F0=9F=9B=9F=20Take=20the=20usage-limit=20reset=20time?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20from=20the=20fleet=20proxy=20when=20the=20CLI=20has=20none?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
When a Claude turn ends in a usage_limit failure and neither the CLI's
rate-limit info nor the 429 text carries a reset time, the Claude adapter
now asks the fleet proxy at ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL (GET /v1/fleet/limits) when
it can next serve the turn's model and stores that as the failure's
resetAt, so the composer banner shows a time and auto-resume can arm.

- A reset time the CLI already reported always wins; the lookup runs only
  for usage_limit failures whose resetAt is still null. The failure message
  is unchanged, and the rate_limit_event notice path is untouched.
- A stop that lands while the lookup is pending still settles the turn as
  interrupted, with no usage_limit failure.
- The proxy answer yields a time only when every Claude credential that is
  neither disabled nor in the error state is blocked: credential-scoped
  cooldowns, cooldowns for the model, and rejected bars that apply to it
  (session_5h, weekly_all, window_*; weekly_fable only for Fable models),
  ignoring passed resets and past timestamps. The earliest-freeing
  credential sets the time; a matching future exclusion can only push it
  later, and a matching permanent exclusion (until null) gives null. Any
  usable credential, no Claude credentials or a malformed body gives null.
- Base URL: Claude settings env ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, then the instance
  environment. Key: ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, then the
  settings apiKeyHelper run with /bin/sh -c in the turn cwd (5 s, 4 KiB
  stdout; skipped on Windows). The request has a 4 s timeout and does not
  follow redirects; the whole lookup is bounded at 6 s. Every failure
  resolves to null and only the outcome is logged at debug level
  (fleet-proxy.limits.reset-at, including reason timeout, failed or defect
  on the outer fallbacks), never the key.
- The adapter receives the HTTP client through a new optional
  fleetProxyHttpClient option; ClaudeDriver passes the server's client, and
  adapters built without it skip the lookup.
- readClaudeApiSettings also reads apiKeyHelper, and readClaudeSettingsEnv delegates to it.

Integration details:
- createClaudeAdapterV2 picks scopedLimitNames, onUsageLimits, modelCatalog and fleetProxyHttpClient, and ClaudeDriver passes both modelCatalog and the server HTTP client.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Upstream #28047 added a promptSuggestions harness option to ClaudeAdapterV2.test.ts beside this commit's fleetProxyHttpClient; both stay. Upstream #33291 and #27753 changed compaction and delegated-task reporting in ClaudeAdapterV2.ts without touching usage-limit reset handling; 965ddc1d6c still has no reset-time fallback for undated usage_limit failures.

